    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter August 15th with an aggressive lineup, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13), who occupies the optimal leadoff spot against McGreevy. His elite sprint speed\u2014a cornerstone of our team strategy\u2014combined with a significant platoon advantage and favorable park factors, makes him our strongest start. **Yordan Alvarez** (70.43) remains a high-floor anchor despite a moderate matchup, buoyed by an elite 0.464 xwOBA. We are also leaning heavily on the top-of-the-order production from **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77) and **Junior Caminero** (67.57), both of whom benefit from prime lineup placement and favorable SP skill differentials. **Kyle Schwarber** (65.94) rounds out our core, utilizing his dynamic platoon edge against the lefty Prielipp to secure a high-efficiency outing.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved keeping **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (43.86) on the bench. He narrowly missed the cut behind **Caleb Durbin** and **Chase Meidroth** due to the stiff matchup against the talented Seymour. While **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** carries a solid 0.385 xwOBA, the combination of his park penalty and the opposing starter\u2019s skill profile ultimately suppressed his efficiency score below our threshold. Conversely, we are tracking **Trea Turner** (62.60) closely; while his matchup is challenging, his elite SB potential remains a critical category-winner, though owners should note the 4% penalty for facing a pitcher who effectively holds runners. No significant weather-related risks are present, but with **Dillon Dingler** (63.75) locked into the 3-hole, we are relying on his recency and platoon advantage to maximize value from the catcher position. All starters should be monitored for late-game defensive substitutions, particularly **Christian Yelich**, whose defensive platoon penalty highlights the volatility in our outfield depth.",
